.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH swarm-key 1  "swarm 0.2.2" "Swarmgit manual"
.SH NAME
swarm\-key \- Key management
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswarm key\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Key management
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
swarm\-key\-recovery(1)
Create a recovery key, name it in the repo, and save it to FILE (keep it offline)
.TP
swarm\-key\-rotate(1)
Move the root to a new key, authorized by the recovery key file
.TP
swarm\-key\-new(1)
Create this machine\*(Aqs own key for a repo, to be authorized by the root
.TP
swarm\-key\-id(1)
Print the key ID of this machine\*(Aqs key for a repo
.TP
swarm\-key\-backup(1)
Copy a repo signing key to FILE with mode 0600
